    | pageurl = http://books.google.com/books?id=9WwiJHkaG2MC&pg=PA18&dq=alicorn
    | passage = The horn of the male [[narwhal]], which sailors called the unicorn of the sea, is thought to have been the unicorn's horn, or '''alicorn''', of medieval commerce. It was very widely believed that '''alicorn''' could be used to detect poisons, and when ground and added to a potion would prevent poisoning.
